          "start_ms": null,
          "status": "needs-review",
          "text": "Description: On January 23, 1983, between 5:15 PM and 5:30 PM, several witnesses observed a gray-black phenomenon in the sky at an estimated altitude of 2500 meters. The object was elongated or in the shape of a \"V\" with no shine. It moved horizontally and silently. Observation through binoculars did not allow for object identification, but according to one witness, a former air navigator, it resembled a trail left by a Boeing 747. The \"V\" shape and the estimated speed (500 to 600 km/h) by the former navigator could support the hypothesis of a plane seen from behind during a descent. It is likely that the witnesses were victims of a misperception with an aircraft, but the latter could not be precisely identified.",
          "translation_text_sha256": "76613e7bfc953f251af573dc688d74ee60c6f3e33cd1f4d506c5f18e5dddfa83"
        }
